// Prism Glass - PluginScanner signature database.
//
// Relaxed JSON: // comments, trailing commas and 'single quotes' are fine. To add your own plugins, do NOT edit this
// file; create  <game dir>/prism/plugin_signatures.json  in the same format and run  .plugins reload .
// An entry there with the same id replaces the bundled one; "remove": ["id"] at the top level drops a bundled one.
//
// One entry = what a plugin looks like from the client. Only id, name and kind are required. All names are lowercase
// except "name" (what is printed).
//
//   id        unique key
//   name      the plugin's real name (also how /version and /plugins print it)
//   kind      anticheat | permissions | admin | protection | world | economy | chat | auth | library | protocol |
//             proxy | software | command-filter | profiler | mod-support | plugin
//   ns        namespaces the plugin registers commands under: "luckperms" for "luckperms:lp" (one hit = high confidence)
//   cmds      distinctive command names, no leading slash ("/wand" for WorldEdit's //wand): one hit is a good sign
//   weak      names other plugins also use: they only add up to a low/medium sign
//   shapes    [{"has": [sub-commands], "min": n}] - a command with at least n of these sub-commands is the plugin even
//             when it was renamed (only visible when the server sends a real Brigadier tree, not Bukkit's "args" blob)
//   channels  plugin-message channels the server pushes: exact "worldedit:cui", prefix "voicechat:" or "fabric*"
//   brand / status / pack   regexes on the server brand, the server-list version text, the resource-pack host
//   ping      anticheats only: "grim" = negative ping ids stepping by one, "transaction" = any ping stream
//   probe     a command that is harmless without arguments (used by the opt-in error probe)
//   priority  higher = probed first
//   builtin   true = ships with the server software (not counted as "the server runs plugins")
//   bukkit    software only: Bukkit-API based, so plugins are possible
